-- Ruled by Meng 2026-11-21, extending L2 (smucclaw/l4-ide#1075): l4 coverage counts. The
-- decision's condition applies two functions at each input, so under
-- --max-steps 1 every input it tries stops at the limit, and the decision
-- is not covered, with the stop as the reason, and a stopped input is never
-- read as one at which the condition raises (both decided by Claude 2026-11-21, pending Meng's review: L2 extension, choice 2).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`double` n MEANS n PLUS n

@export Which band a number falls into.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`band` n MEANS
  BRANCH
    IF `double` (`double` n) GREATER THAN 100 THEN 2
    OTHERWISE                                       1
